@startuml
!include ../docs/images/common-sequence.iuml

title Message Processor — Period Counter Reset Mechanism

box "Message Processor" $OnPrem
    participant "Processor" as Processor
end box

box "Redis" $OnPrem
    database "metrics:message_processor:\n{id}:{counter}:{period}" as Counter
end box

== Startup, once ==

Processor -> Counter++ : **Reset the lifetime counters**\n""DEL registration_misses:lifetime, operator_misses:lifetime, total_messages_processed:lifetime""
Counter --> Processor-- : OK
note right of Processor
    "lifetime" means "since this process instance
    started," not "forever" -- Redis is a separate,
    persistent service, so a restart alone doesn't
    clear these keys for free.
end note

== Hot path — every message, zero Redis I/O ==

loop for each consumed message
    Processor -> Processor : **Record a message processed**\n""self._total_messages_processed.record()""
    opt aircraft enrichment misses
        Processor -> Processor : **Record a registration miss**\n""self._registration_misses.record()""
    end
    opt operator enrichment misses
        Processor -> Processor : **Record an operator miss**\n""self._operator_misses.record()""
    end
end
note over Processor
    record() is pure in-memory arithmetic under a
    lock -- no accumulator here ever calls Redis.
end note

== Independently, every telemetry_interval_seconds (telemetry thread) ==

loop for each of the three accumulators
    Processor -> Processor : **Take and zero the pending delta**\n""delta = accumulator.flush_and_reset()""
    alt delta == 0
        Processor -> Processor : **Skip this metric this cycle**
    else delta > 0
        loop for hour, today (not lifetime)
            Processor -> Processor : **Compute the real UTC boundary**\n""expires_at = next_period_boundary(period, now)""
            Processor -> Counter++ : **Atomically increment and conditionally expire**\n""EVALSHA incr_period_counter.lua 0 key delta expires_at""
            alt key did not already exist
                Counter -> Counter : **Set expiry to the real boundary**\n""EXPIREAT key expires_at""
            else key already existed this period
                Counter -> Counter : **Leave the existing expiry untouched**\n""-- never slides the window forward --""
            end
            Counter --> Processor-- : new_value
        end
        Processor -> Counter++ : **Increment the lifetime total (never expires)**\n""INCRBY key delta""
        Counter --> Processor-- : new_value
    end
end

note over Counter
    core-health (not this component) reads these keys
    and publishes them over MQTT/Home Assistant, using
    the exact topic paths/unique_id this component's own
    telemetry publisher would otherwise have used -- see
    core-health/README.md's "Counter mimicry" section.
end note

@enduml
